Z||000000||AusFiero||08-14-2001||09:19 PM||||Ok I was going to keep this under wraps until I could afford to produce it. We are talking at least 1 year away if things go well for me with bodykits etc. But what the hell. This will possibly be in production then for around a retail price of US$4500. Will be designed to be fitted in a weekend or 2 by the average home handyman.<P>Styling is actually a little bit of Ferarri, a little bit of Holden, a bit of stage 2 body kit and bits and pieces just chucked in from my imagination, making it a real mongrel. Hmmm may even be a good name for it. Ok lets just call it The Mongrel.<P>Comments before I commit to something like this?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rebody001.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||6
Z||000001||qwikgta||08-14-2001||09:28 PM||||At a quick glance I was not sure if it had a large dent on the side over the front wheel all the way to the door, but then I looked again and I guess it is the way you have it lighted.  Now I do like it.  Are you going to include some type of brace for the undercarrage or is it up to us to get that done??<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents. <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject</A> <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.vafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.vafieros.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
